    "Three times one is three. Four times two is eight. The answer is three eighths.": {"src":"/fractions/audio/ryan-08762d0e0f132f6a.mp3","words":[{"atMs":100,"durationMs":359,"text":"Three"},{"atMs":472.3,"durationMs":385.6,"text":"times"},{"atMs":871.3,"durationMs":266,"text":"one"},{"atMs":1150.5,"durationMs":186.2,"text":"is"},{"atMs":1350,"durationMs":465.4,"text":"three"},{"atMs":2736.2,"durationMs":212.8,"text":"Four"},{"atMs":2962.2,"durationMs":398.9,"text":"times"},{"atMs":3374.5,"durationMs":239.4,"text":"two"},{"atMs":3627.1,"durationMs":172.9,"text":"is"},{"atMs":3813.3,"durationMs":372.3,"text":"eight"},{"atMs":5103.2,"durationMs":199.5,"text":"The"},{"atMs":5316,"durationMs":465.4,"text":"answer"},{"atMs":5794.7,"durationMs":186.2,"text":"is"},{"atMs":5994.2,"durationMs":305.8,"text":"three"},{"atMs":6313.3,"durationMs":531.9,"text":"eighths"}],"durationMs":6845},
